# {{ .name }}

An Intropy extractor. Each run sweeps the `{{ .port }}` source port once,
runs every file through an extractor pipeline (deserialize, validate,
idempotency check, transform) and publishes the result as the
`{{ .publishes }}` message on the system's pub/sub (topic `{{ .channel }}`).
A published file is deleted; a failed one stays for the next run. In
production it runs as a CronJob.
{{- if .empty }}

The pipeline steps were scaffolded empty: each throws
`NotImplementedException` until it is implemented.
{{- end }}

## Build and test

```bash
task build
task test
```

The extractor does not run standalone. Run it with the rest of the system
from the system host (`task run` there), which runs it once at startup.

## Container image

```bash
docker build --build-context contracts=../{{ .contracts }} -t {{ .appId }} .
```

See `AGENTS.md` for the component's names, ports and key files, and
<https://docs.intropy.io> for how extractors work.
